## Conclusion

In this hands-on, you've seen how to use PEEx to augment your unit tests with automatic mutation and fuzzing. This approach significantly enhances the quality of the tests by discovering edge cases that previously have been missing. In the end, gaining valuable insights into the robustness of your methods, even before running your tests.

Keep in mind that the results will vary depending on your specific scenario and the complexity of your methods, as fuzz testing always has its limits and in some cases might result in edge cases that are not covered by typical and representative scenarios.

In this way, tests' quality is increased, and you as a developer gain a bit more confidence and efficiency in your coding process.

